IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc22-counts.l4 -- sections 581 to 588 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (Part XX: general provisions respecting counts, special provisions respecting counts, particulars, ownership of property).
-- Part agent ccc22. Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE (the text's own words bring the case within the rule); JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Tags in the comments: [M-a] a failed "if"/"where" or a flat negative counted as the text's no; [M-b] a prohibition or grant limited by its own wording counted as NOT the text's no (NOTHING);
-- [F:...] a fork line for NOTES.md (may-if, may-where, entitled, duty, unless). Section 2 terms and other parts' answers are INPUTS named for their section.
-- The sufficiency provisions (ss 583 to 586) are written as "the omission alone renders the count insufficient": JUST FALSE where the text says it does not.

§ `Section 581 -- General provisions respecting counts`

-- src:12594 | 581 (1) Each count in an indictment shall in general apply to a single transaction and shall contain in substance a statement that the accused or defendant committed an offence therein specified.
@ref s 581(1) (src:12594-12594)
GIVEN `the count applies to a single transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the count contains in substance a statement that the accused or defendant committed an offence therein specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 581(1) the count is in the form subsection (1) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the count contains in substance a statement that the accused or defendant committed an offence therein specified` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall contain in substance a statement that the accused or defendant committed an offence therein specified" [M-a] [F:duty]
        IF NOT `the count applies to a single transaction` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall in general apply to a single transaction"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12596 | (2) The statement referred to in subsection (1) may be
-- src:12597 | (a) in popular language without technical averments or allegations of matters that are not essential to be proved;
-- src:12598 | (b) in the words of the enactment that describes the offence or declares the matters charged to be an indictable offence; or
-- src:12599 | (c) in words that are sufficient to give to the accused notice of the offence with which he is charged.
@ref s 581(2) (src:12596-12599)
DECLARE `s 581(2) the form of the statement` IS ONE OF
    `s 581(2)(a) popular language without technical averments or allegations of matters that are not essential to be proved`
    `s 581(2)(b) the words of the enactment that describes the offence or declares the matters charged to be an indictable offence`
    `s 581(2)(c) words that are sufficient to give to the accused notice of the offence with which he is charged`
    `s 581(2) some other form`

-- src:12596 | (2) The statement referred to in subsection (1) may be
-- src:12597 | (a) in popular language without technical averments or allegations of matters that are not essential to be proved;
-- src:12598 | (b) in the words of the enactment that describes the offence or declares the matters charged to be an indictable offence; or
-- src:12599 | (c) in words that are sufficient to give to the accused notice of the offence with which he is charged.
@ref s 581(2) (src:12596-12599)
GIVEN form IS A `s 581(2) the form of the statement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 581(2) the statement may be in this form` MEANS
    IF form EQUALS `s 581(2) some other form`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be (a) in popular language ...; (b) in the words of the enactment ...; or (c) in words that are sufficient"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:12601 | (3) A count shall contain sufficient detail of the circumstances of the alleged offence to give to the accused reasonable information with respect to the act or omission to be proved against him and to identify the transaction referred to, but otherwise the absence or insufficiency of details does not vitiate the count.
@ref s 581(3) (src:12601-12601)
GIVEN `the detail gives the accused reasonable information with respect to the act or omission to be proved against them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the detail identifies the transaction referred to` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 581(3) the count contains sufficient detail of the circumstances of the alleged offence` MEANS
    IF `the detail gives the accused reasonable information with respect to the act or omission to be proved against them` AND `the detail identifies the transaction referred to`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A count shall contain sufficient detail of the circumstances of the alleged offence to give to the accused reasonable information with respect to the act or omission to be proved against him and to identify the transaction referred to" [M-a] [F:duty]

-- (3), "but otherwise the absence or insufficiency of details does not vitiate the count": the answer is whether the absence or insufficiency vitiates the count.
-- src:12601 | (3) A count shall contain sufficient detail of the circumstances of the alleged offence to give to the accused reasonable information with respect to the act or omission to be proved against him and to identify the transaction referred to, but otherwise the absence or insufficiency of details does not vitiate the count.
@ref s 581(3) (src:12601-12601)
GIVEN `the count gives the accused reasonable information and identifies the transaction referred to` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 581(3) the absence or insufficiency of details vitiates the count` MEANS
    IF `the count gives the accused reasonable information and identifies the transaction referred to`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but otherwise the absence or insufficiency of details does not vitiate the count" [M-a]
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "but otherwise" (the saving applies only to a count that gives reasonable information and identifies the transaction; the subsection does not say such a count is vitiated)

-- src:12603 | (4) If an accused is charged with an offence under section 47 or sections 50 to 53, every overt act that is to be relied on shall be stated in the indictment.
@ref s 581(4) (src:12603-12603)
GIVEN `the offence charged` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `every overt act that is to be relied on is stated in the indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 581(4) the indictment states every overt act to be relied on` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 47 OR (`the offence charged`'s `section` AT LEAST 50 AND `the offence charged`'s `section` AT MOST 53)) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an accused is charged with an offence under section 47 or sections 50 to 53"
        IF `every overt act that is to be relied on is stated in the indictment` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "every overt act that is to be relied on shall be stated in the indictment" [M-a] [F:duty]

-- src:12605 | (5) A count may refer to any section, subsection, paragraph or subparagraph of the enactment that creates the offence charged, and for the purpose of determining whether a count is sufficient, consideration shall be given to any such reference.
@ref s 581(5) (src:12605-12605)
GIVEN `the provision is a section, subsection, paragraph or subparagraph of the enactment that creates the offence charged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 581(5) the count may refer to the provision` MEANS
    IF `the provision is a section, subsection, paragraph or subparagraph of the enactment that creates the offence charged`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any section, subsection, paragraph or subparagraph of the enactment that creates the offence charged"

-- src:12605 | (5) A count may refer to any section, subsection, paragraph or subparagraph of the enactment that creates the offence charged, and for the purpose of determining whether a count is sufficient, consideration shall be given to any such reference.
@ref s 581(5) (src:12605-12605)
GIVEN `the count refers to a section, subsection, paragraph or subparagraph of the enactment that creates the offence charged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 581(5) the reference is considered in determining whether the count is sufficient` MEANS
    IF `the count refers to a section, subsection, paragraph or subparagraph of the enactment that creates the offence charged`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of "any such reference"

-- (6): "Nothing in this Part relating to matters that do not render a count insufficient shall be deemed to restrict or limit the application of this section." The answer: does the provision restrict section 581?
-- src:12607 | (6) Nothing in this Part relating to matters that do not render a count insufficient shall be deemed to restrict or limit the application of this section.
@ref s 581(6) (src:12607-12607)
GIVEN `the provision of this Part relates to matters that do not render a count insufficient` IS A BOOLEAN
