§ `Section 582 -- High treason and first degree murder`

-- src:12609 | 582 No person shall be convicted for the offence of high treason or first degree murder unless in the indictment charging the offence he is specifically charged with that offence.
@ref s 582 (src:12609-12609)
GIVEN `the offence is high treason or first degree murder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the indictment charging the offence the person is specifically charged with that offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 582 the section bars a conviction for high treason or first degree murder` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offence is high treason or first degree murder` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the offence of high treason or first degree murder"
        IF `in the indictment charging the offence the person is specifically charged with that offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall be convicted for the offence of high treason or first degree murder unless in the indictment charging the offence he is specifically charged with that offence" [F:unless] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 583 -- Certain omissions not grounds for objection`

-- src:12611 | 583 No count in an indictment is insufficient by reason of the absence of details where, in the opinion of the court, the count otherwise fulfils the requirements of section 581 and, without restricting the generality of the foregoing, no count in an indictment is insufficient by reason only that
@ref s 583 (src:12611-12611)
GIVEN `in the opinion of the court the count otherwise fulfils the requirements of section 581` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 583 the absence of details renders the count insufficient` MEANS
    IF `in the opinion of the court the count otherwise fulfils the requirements of section 581`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No count in an indictment is insufficient by reason of the absence of details where, in the opinion of the court, the count otherwise fulfils the requirements of section 581" [M-a]
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where, in the opinion of the court, the count otherwise fulfils the requirements of section 581"

-- src:12611 | 583 No count in an indictment is insufficient by reason of the absence of details where, in the opinion of the court, the count otherwise fulfils the requirements of section 581 and, without restricting the generality of the foregoing, no count in an indictment is insufficient by reason only that
-- src:12612 | (a) it does not name the person injured or intended or attempted to be injured;
-- src:12613 | (b) it does not name the person who owns or has a special property or interest in property mentioned in the count;
-- src:12614 | (c) it charges an intent to defraud without naming or describing the person whom it was intended to defraud;
-- src:12615 | (d) it does not set out any writing that is the subject of the charge;
-- src:12616 | (e) it does not set out the words used where words that are alleged to have been used are the subject of the charge;
-- src:12617 | (f) it does not specify the means by which the alleged offence was committed;
-- src:12618 | (g) it does not name or describe with precision any person, place or thing; or
-- src:12619 | (h) it does not, where the consent of a person, official or authority is required before proceedings may be instituted for an offence, state that the consent has been obtained.
@ref s 583 (src:12611-12619)
DECLARE `s 583 the omission` IS ONE OF
    `s 583(a) it does not name the person injured or intended or attempted to be injured`
    `s 583(b) it does not name the person who owns or has a special property or interest in property mentioned in the count`
    `s 583(c) it charges an intent to defraud without naming or describing the person whom it was intended to defraud`
    `s 583(d) it does not set out any writing that is the subject of the charge`
    `s 583(e) it does not set out the words used where words that are alleged to have been used are the subject of the charge`
    `s 583(f) it does not specify the means by which the alleged offence was committed`
    `s 583(g) it does not name or describe with precision any person, place or thing`
    `s 583(h) it does not, where the consent of a person, official or authority is required before proceedings may be instituted for an offence, state that the consent has been obtained`
    `s 583 some other omission`

-- src:12611 | 583 No count in an indictment is insufficient by reason of the absence of details where, in the opinion of the court, the count otherwise fulfils the requirements of section 581 and, without restricting the generality of the foregoing, no count in an indictment is insufficient by reason only that
-- src:12612 | (a) it does not name the person injured or intended or attempted to be injured;
-- src:12613 | (b) it does not name the person who owns or has a special property or interest in property mentioned in the count;
-- src:12614 | (c) it charges an intent to defraud without naming or describing the person whom it was intended to defraud;
-- src:12615 | (d) it does not set out any writing that is the subject of the charge;
-- src:12616 | (e) it does not set out the words used where words that are alleged to have been used are the subject of the charge;
-- src:12617 | (f) it does not specify the means by which the alleged offence was committed;
-- src:12618 | (g) it does not name or describe with precision any person, place or thing; or
-- src:12619 | (h) it does not, where the consent of a person, official or authority is required before proceedings may be instituted for an offence, state that the consent has been obtained.
@ref s 583 (src:12611-12619)
GIVEN omission IS A `s 583 the omission`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 583 the omission alone renders the count insufficient` MEANS
    IF omission EQUALS `s 583 some other omission`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "without restricting the generality of the foregoing" (the list of (a) to (h) is illustrative)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no count in an indictment is insufficient by reason only that" [M-a]

§ `Section 584 -- Sufficiency of count charging libel`

-- src:12623 | 584 (1) No count for publishing a seditious or defamatory libel, or for selling or exhibiting an obscene book, pamphlet, newspaper or other written matter, is insufficient by reason only that it does not set out the words that are alleged to be libellous or the writing that is alleged to be obscene.
@ref s 584(1) (src:12623-12623)
GIVEN `the count is for publishing a seditious or defamatory libel, or for selling or exhibiting an obscene book, pamphlet, newspaper or other written matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only omission is that it does not set out the words alleged to be libellous or the writing alleged to be obscene` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 584(1) the omission alone renders the count insufficient` MEANS
    IF `the count is for publishing a seditious or defamatory libel, or for selling or exhibiting an obscene book, pamphlet, newspaper or other written matter` AND `the only omission is that it does not set out the words alleged to be libellous or the writing alleged to be obscene`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is insufficient by reason only that it does not set out the words that are alleged to be libellous or the writing that is alleged to be obscene" [M-a]
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No count for publishing a seditious or defamatory libel, or for selling or exhibiting an obscene book, pamphlet, newspaper or other written matter"

-- src:12625 | (2) A count for publishing a libel may charge that the published matter was written in a sense that by innuendo made the publication thereof criminal, and may specify that sense without any introductory assertion to show how the matter was written in that sense.
@ref s 584(2) (src:12625-12625)
GIVEN `the count is for publishing a libel` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 584(2) the count may charge that the published matter was written in a sense that by innuendo made the publication criminal` MEANS
    IF `the count is for publishing a libel`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A count for publishing a libel may charge"

-- src:12627 | (3) It is sufficient, on the trial of a count for publishing a libel, to prove that the matter published was libellous, with or without innuendo.
@ref s 584(3) (src:12627-12627)
GIVEN `the trial is of a count for publishing a libel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that the matter published was libellous, with or without innuendo` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 584(3) proof that the matter published was libellous is sufficient` MEANS
    IF `the trial is of a count for publishing a libel` AND `it is proved that the matter published was libellous, with or without innuendo`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is sufficient, on the trial of a count for publishing a libel, to prove that the matter published was libellous"

§ `Section 585 -- Sufficiency of count charging perjury, etc.`

-- src:12629 | 585 No count that charges
-- src:12630 | (a) perjury,
-- src:12631 | (b) the making of a false oath or a false statement,
-- src:12632 | (c) fabricating evidence, or
-- src:12633 | (d) procuring the commission of an offence mentioned in paragraph (a), (b) or (c),
-- src:12634 | is insufficient by reason only that it does not state the nature of the authority of the tribunal before which the oath or statement was taken or made, or the subject of the inquiry, or the words used or the evidence fabricated, or that it does not expressly negative the truth of the words used.
@ref s 585 (src:12629-12634)
DECLARE `s 585 the charge` IS ONE OF
    `s 585(a) perjury`
    `s 585(b) the making of a false oath or a false statement`
    `s 585(c) fabricating evidence`
    `s 585(d) procuring the commission of an offence mentioned in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)`
    `s 585 some other charge`

-- src:12629 | 585 No count that charges
-- src:12630 | (a) perjury,
-- src:12631 | (b) the making of a false oath or a false statement,
-- src:12632 | (c) fabricating evidence, or
-- src:12633 | (d) procuring the commission of an offence mentioned in paragraph (a), (b) or (c),
-- src:12634 | is insufficient by reason only that it does not state the nature of the authority of the tribunal before which the oath or statement was taken or made, or the subject of the inquiry, or the words used or the evidence fabricated, or that it does not expressly negative the truth of the words used.
@ref s 585 (src:12629-12634)
DECLARE `s 585 the omission` IS ONE OF
    `s 585 it does not state the nature of the authority of the tribunal before which the oath or statement was taken or made`
    `s 585 it does not state the subject of the inquiry`
    `s 585 it does not state the words used or the evidence fabricated`
    `s 585 it does not expressly negative the truth of the words used`
    `s 585 some other omission`

-- src:12629 | 585 No count that charges
-- src:12630 | (a) perjury,
-- src:12631 | (b) the making of a false oath or a false statement,
-- src:12632 | (c) fabricating evidence, or
-- src:12633 | (d) procuring the commission of an offence mentioned in paragraph (a), (b) or (c),
-- src:12634 | is insufficient by reason only that it does not state the nature of the authority of the tribunal before which the oath or statement was taken or made, or the subject of the inquiry, or the words used or the evidence fabricated, or that it does not expressly negative the truth of the words used.
@ref s 585 (src:12629-12634)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 585 the charge`
      omission IS A `s 585 the omission`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 585 the omission alone renders the count insufficient` MEANS
    IF charge EQUALS `s 585 some other charge` OR omission EQUALS `s 585 some other omission`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No count that charges (a) perjury, (b) the making of a false oath or a false statement, (c) fabricating evidence, or (d) procuring ..." and the four omissions it names
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is insufficient by reason only that it does not state the nature of the authority of the tribunal" [M-a]

§ `Section 586 -- Sufficiency of count relating to fraud`

-- src:12636 | 586 No count that alleges false pretences, fraud or any attempt or conspiracy by fraudulent means is insufficient by reason only that it does not set out in detail the nature of the false pretence, fraud or fraudulent means.
@ref s 586 (src:12636-12636)
GIVEN `the count alleges false pretences, fraud or any attempt or conspiracy by fraudulent means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only omission is that it does not set out in detail the nature of the false pretence, fraud or fraudulent means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 586 the omission alone renders the count insufficient` MEANS
    IF `the count alleges false pretences, fraud or any attempt or conspiracy by fraudulent means` AND `the only omission is that it does not set out in detail the nature of the false pretence, fraud or fraudulent means`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is insufficient by reason only that it does not set out in detail the nature of the false pretence, fraud or fraudulent means" [M-a]
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No count that alleges false pretences, fraud or any attempt or conspiracy by fraudulent means"

§ `Section 587 -- Particulars`

-- (1): a court may, where it is satisfied that it is necessary for a fair trial, order the prosecutor to furnish particulars.
-- src:12640 | 587 (1) A court may, where it is satisfied that it is necessary for a fair trial, order the prosecutor to furnish particulars and, without restricting the generality of the foregoing, may order the prosecutor to furnish particulars
@ref s 587(1) (src:12640-12640)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that it is necessary for a fair trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 587(1) the court may order the prosecutor to furnish particulars` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that it is necessary for a fair trial`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A court may, where it is satisfied that it is necessary for a fair trial, order the prosecutor to furnish particulars" [F:may-where] [M-a]

-- src:12641 | (a) of what is relied on in support of a charge of perjury, the making of a false oath or a false statement, fabricating evidence or counselling the commission of any of those offences;
-- src:12642 | (b) of any false pretence or fraud that is alleged;
-- src:12643 | (c) of any alleged attempt or conspiracy by fraudulent means;
-- src:12644 | (d) setting out the passages in a book, pamphlet, newspaper or other printing or writing that are relied on in support of a charge of selling or exhibiting an obscene book, pamphlet, newspaper, printing or writing;
-- src:12645 | (e) further describing any writing or words that are the subject of a charge;
-- src:12646 | (f) further describing the means by which an offence is alleged to have been committed; or
-- src:12647 | (g) further describing a person, place or thing referred to in an indictment.
@ref s 587(1) (src:12641-12647)
DECLARE `s 587(1) the particulars` IS ONE OF
    `s 587(1)(a) of what is relied on in support of a charge of perjury, the making of a false oath or a false statement, fabricating evidence or counselling the commission of any of those offences`
    `s 587(1)(b) of any false pretence or fraud that is alleged`
    `s 587(1)(c) of any alleged attempt or conspiracy by fraudulent means`
    `s 587(1)(d) setting out the passages in a book, pamphlet, newspaper or other printing or writing that are relied on in support of a charge of selling or exhibiting an obscene book`
    `s 587(1)(e) further describing any writing or words that are the subject of a charge`
    `s 587(1)(f) further describing the means by which an offence is alleged to have been committed`
    `s 587(1)(g) further describing a person, place or thing referred to in an indictment`
    `s 587(1) some other particulars`

-- src:12641 | (a) of what is relied on in support of a charge of perjury, the making of a false oath or a false statement, fabricating evidence or counselling the commission of any of those offences;
-- src:12642 | (b) of any false pretence or fraud that is alleged;
