      consequence IS A `s 587(3) the consequence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 587(3) the consequence follows where a particular is delivered` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a particular is delivered pursuant to section 587` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a particular is delivered pursuant to this section" [M-a]
        IF consequence EQUALS `s 587(3) some other consequence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "(a) a copy shall be given ...; (b) the particular shall be entered in the record; and (c) the trial shall proceed"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 588 -- Ownership`

-- src:12658 | 588 The real and personal property of which a person has, by law, the management, control or custody shall, for the purposes of an indictment or proceeding against any other person for an offence committed on or in respect of the property, be deemed to be the property of the person who has the management, control or custody of it.
@ref s 588 (src:12658-12658)
GIVEN `s 2 property: the thing is real or personal property` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has, by law, the management, control or custody of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the indictment or proceeding is against any other person for an offence committed on or in respect of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 588 the property is deemed to be the property of the person who has the management, control or custody of it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 property: the thing is real or personal property` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the thing is property is for s 2 "property", which the keel answers
        IF `s 2 property: the thing is real or personal property` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The real and personal property"
        IF `the person has, by law, the management, control or custody of it` AND `the indictment or proceeding is against any other person for an offence committed on or in respect of the property` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purposes of an indictment or proceeding against any other person for an offence committed on or in respect of the property"
